}_{0}^{6}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(\\frac{x}{3})}^{2}+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}}\\cdot (3\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =12{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡u{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2-12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2 \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+\\sqrt{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364804 1000 #edb/ref 17592186364805 13194139535752 true] [17592186364804 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535752 true] [17592186364804 1041 "field-1" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364804 1104 #edb/ref 17592186364805 13194139535752 true] [17592186364804 1110 #uuid "981baf1d-c3e3-5884-8c17-781894d4c162" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364805 1034 "12\\ln(2+\\sqrt{5})" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364805 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535752 true] [17592186364805 1111 #uuid "03ce8b69-a178-5bce-9f24-76b01c0c8615" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1017 #edb/ref 17592186364807 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1089 "q-95689" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1100 "$\\int \\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{{e}^{2x}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1113 #uuid "1cc17f63-e50c-556b-8900-7b2cf2330aa9" 13194139535752 true] [17592186364806 1145 "This integral resembles the basic integral for the inverse hyperbolic cosine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${e}^{2x}={({e}^{x})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u={e}^{x}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and compute it, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\